{"source_key":"sha256-1b040a14b56f8e8c10dd28d48155f19f","record_index":316,"record_hash":"sha256:e3a2d0cd75fee8d0272574544e015f0781bafd665ff40b52ef398eca70088bfe","timestamp":"2026-07-09T12:15:10.669Z","kind":"message","source_event_kind":"codex:response_item:message","role":"assistant","text":"I looked through `caleb/single-branch-project-starting` without switching the worktree. The branch adds the right foundation for the app: metadata-only project init via [crates/but-workspace/src/init.rs]([REDACTED:path]), exposed through [crates/but-api/src/workspace.rs]([REDACTED:path]), Tauri/server/SDK, and UI paths that keep the user on the current branch.\n\nWhat’s still missing for CLI readiness is all in `crates/but`. `git diff origin/master...caleb/single-branch-project-starting -- crates/but` is empty, and current `but setup` still does managed-workspace setup: it calls `set_base_branch_with_perm` at [crates/but/src/command/legacy/setup.rs]([REDACTED:path]), then switches to `gitbutler/workspace` at [crates/but/src/command/legacy/setup.rs]([REDACTED:path]), installs managed hooks, and prints workspace-branch copy.\n\nMinimal path I’d ship:\n\n1. Add `but setup --single-branch [--init] [--target <remote/branch>]`, not a new command tree.\n2. Add/reuse a permission-taking API helper, e.g. `but_api::workspace::set_target_ref_and_init_project_with_perm(...)`, so CLI can call it while already holding `RepoExclusive` instead of using the self-locking wrapper.\n3. Split `setup::repo` so target discovery/`gb-local` creation is shared, but the single-branch path skips `set_base_branch_with_perm`, `switch_back_to_workspace_with_perm`, managed hook install, and workspace-branch messaging.\n4. Make [check_project_setup]([REDACTED:path]) mode-aware. Right now it rejects any non-`gitbutler/*` HEAD, so a single-branch setup would be “repaired” back into workspace mode by later CLI commands.\n5. Route `but config target` through the metadata-only path in single-branch mode; it still calls legacy `set_base_branch` at [crates/but/src/command/config.rs]([REDACTED:path]).\n\nOne correctness thing I would fix before calling it ready: [set_target_ref_and_init_project]([REDACTED:path]) preserves an existing `target_commit_id` even when the target ref changes, and the test locks that in at [crates/but-workspace/tests/workspace/init.rs]([REDACTED:path]). That is fine for idempotent init, but risky for real target switching. Lazy fix: preserve it only when the requested target ref matches the stored one; otherwise recompute merge-base.\n\nValidation I ran:\n`git diff --check origin/master...caleb/single-branch-project-starting` passed.\n`cargo test -p but-workspace --test workspace fresh_init_sets_target_and_keeps_current_branch` passed.\n`cargo test -p but-api set_target_ref_accepts_remote_tracking_ref_and_persists_metadata` passed.\n\nSkipped: broad CLI implementation and new snapshots, because this was an investigation pass.\n\n<oai-mem-citation>\n<citation_entries>\nMEMORY.md:1-44|note=[repo validation and API exposure guidance]\n<[REDACTED:path]>\n<rollout_ids>\n[REDACTED:entropy]\n<[REDACTED:path]>\n<[REDACTED:path]>","tool_name":null,"tool_input":null,"source_record":{"timestamp":"2026-07-09T12:15:10.669Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"message","id":"[REDACTED:entropy]","role":"assistant","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"[REDACTED:entropy]"},"phase":"final_answer"}}}